<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Cart</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>hire cart
put &lt;log or ore&gt; in cart
unload cart
hitch cart to horse
unhitch cart
</pre>
<p>Calvin the carpenter on Colosseum Square in Midgaard hires out a cart with 
a draught horse (<a cmd='#'>hire cart</a>). They wait for you on the square, hitched, 
and stay yours, wherever you leave them, until the next reboot brings them 
back to him. You have one at a time: hire another, and his lad fetches 
the old pair, leaving whatever was in the cart where it stood. Only you 
can mount the horse: <a cmd='#'>mount horse</a>, and ride where you like; the cart 
follows.
</p><p>A cart holds a dozen logs or more loads of ore. <a cmd='#'>put log in cart</a> heaves 
up a log or load lying on the ground, which takes some endurance. By 
John the Lumberjack or Sam the blacksmith, <a cmd='#'>unload cart</a> hands them 
everything in it, even from the saddle; each piece counts for whoever 
felled or mined it.
</p><p>Friends can climb in (<a cmd='#'>enter cart</a>) and ride along, though they take up 
room the cargo could have had.
</p><p><a cmd='#'>unhitch cart</a> leaves the cart standing; <a cmd='#'>hitch cart to horse</a> hitches it 
again, to the draught horse or another horse.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Fell</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Mine</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Houses</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Mount</a>
</pre>




</div>